# Context Graph for the Context Graph repository itself.
# Modules and containment were bootstrapped by ctx init; constraints and concepts are the design's own rules.

# ---- mappings: most specific first --------------------------------------------
M src/adapters/claude-code/**  L:claude-code
M src/adapters/codex/**        L:codex
M src/adapters/**              L:adapters
M src/bench/**                 L:bench
M src/cli/**                   L:cli
M src/core/**                  L:core
M src/embed/**                 L:embed
M src/gate/**                  L:gate
M src/graph/**                 L:graph
M src/hygiene/**               L:hygiene
M src/index/**                 L:index
M src/init/**                  L:init
M src/mcp/**                   L:mcp
M src/observe/**               L:observe
M src/overlay/**               L:overlay
M src/record/**                L:record
M src/util/**                  L:util
M src/walker/**                L:walker
M src/**                       L:src
M view/**                      L:view
M packs/**                     L:packs
M adapters/**                  L:packaging
M docs/**                      L:docs
M **                           L:repo

# ---- logical nodes --------------------------------------------------------------
L L:repo         Context Graph repository
L L:src          Plugin source
L L:graph        The .ctx grammar: parser, validator, writer, active set
L L:walker       Deterministic walk and slice rendering
L L:observe      Observation: shell and patch parsers, store, coverage, replay
L L:index        Import graph and symbol lookup
L L:record       Decision recording, loop guard, provenance
L L:adapters     Harness adapters: shared core plus per-harness profiles
L L:claude-code  Claude Code profile
L L:codex        Codex profile
L L:mcp          The pull surface
L L:core         Repository context and configuration
L L:cli          Command line entrypoint and lazily loaded command modules
L L:gate         Merge gate
L L:init         Bootstrap, packs, conformance, ratification
L L:hygiene      Retirement, archival, hygiene report, timeline
L L:overlay      Event server, client, hosted mode
L L:embed        Embedding provider, chunker, vector store, hints
L L:bench        Replay benchmark
L L:util         Paths, git, tokens, toml
L L:view         Synapse view, browser app
L L:packs        Style packs
L L:packaging    Harness plugin directories
L L:docs         Design specification and research

# ---- concepts ---------------------------------------------------------------------
C C:floor-and-pull   The walker sets the floor deterministically; the agent pulls above it through the query surface
C C:git-is-truth     The graph lives in git; a live overlay is only ever provisional state
C C:never-delete     Records are superseded, retired, or archived, never deleted; the ledger is the proof a decision was made
C C:harness-agnostic Harness differences live in a profile; everything else is shared

# ---- containment ---------------------------------------------------------------------
E L:claude-code in L:adapters
E L:codex in L:adapters
E L:adapters in L:src
E L:bench in L:src
E L:cli in L:src
E L:core in L:src
E L:embed in L:src
E L:gate in L:src
E L:graph in L:src
E L:hygiene in L:src
E L:index in L:src
E L:init in L:src
E L:mcp in L:src
E L:observe in L:src
E L:overlay in L:src
E L:record in L:src
E L:util in L:src
E L:walker in L:src
E L:src in L:repo
E L:view in L:repo
E L:packs in L:repo
E L:packaging in L:repo
E L:docs in L:repo

# ---- what implements what ---------------------------------------------------------------
E L:walker impl C:floor-and-pull
E L:mcp impl C:floor-and-pull
E L:overlay impl C:git-is-truth
E L:graph impl C:never-delete
E L:hygiene impl C:never-delete
E L:adapters impl C:harness-agnostic

# ---- enforced ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
K E walker.pure L:walker the walker and slice renderer import nothing that touches the network, a model, a process, or the overlay; the applicable set is a pure function of graph and path test:src/walker/boundary.test.ts

# ---- guided ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
K G walker.floor-then-pull  L:walker    the slice is a deterministic floor; anything a model chooses to fetch is a reach event, never a change to the applicable set
K G walker.hints-last       L:walker    hint lines render after decisions and are the first dropped under budget; they never become must lines
K G adapters.profile-only   L:adapters  a harness profile supplies edit tools, input shapes, and response shapes; the hook flow lives in core.ts and is never duplicated per harness
K G overlay.bounded         L:overlay   nothing on the edit path waits on the server without a timeout, and a missing server changes nothing but the live lines
K G graph.active-set        L:graph     the walker reads only the active set; the archive is read by history, the gate, and the view
K G hygiene.proposes        L:hygiene   hygiene proposes and a person retires; gc moves only records that are already inactive
K G embed.hints-only        L:embed     retrieval results render as hint lines below constraints and are the first thing dropped under budget
K G observe.no-contents     L:observe   observation events carry paths, ranges, and modes, never file contents
K G cli.lazy-commands       L:cli       lifecycle and runtime commands load on demand so the hook path never pays for them
K G record.why-points       L:record    a decision's why must point at a constraint or concept; a why that points at nothing is rejected
K G packaging.script-dirs   L:packaging plugin scripts resolve the CLI relative to their own directory, never through a global install
